    "title": "Flyers girls place first at Sauk Centre cross-country race - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Brian Bowman ,\n14 hours ago The Little Falls Flyers girls’ cross-country team continues to impress after running to a first-place finish out of 10 teams at the Sauk Centre Mainstreeter Invite at the Lynx National Golf Course on Tuesday, Sept. 30.\nLittle Falls’ Rose Jarnot finished third with an impressive time of 19:59.8 while the Flyers’ Malin Youngberg was fourth at 20:03.2.\nLittle Falls’ other results included Haddlie Dobis (fifth, 20:07.2), Grace LeClair (11th, 20:32.4), Peyton Hoheisel (14th, 20:55.1), Breckon Hoheisel (21st, 21:47.6), and Maggie Graeve (39th, 23:38.3).\nLittle Falls was seven points better than second-place New London-Spicer.\nOn the boys’ side, Blake Nolan ran a solid eighth-place 18:24.2 to lead Little Falls to a fourth-place finish.\nThe Flyers’ other results included Noah Cameron (12th, 18:38.5), Kobi Cameron (21st, 19:30.8), Judah Meyer (25th, 19:36.6), Sean Derry (34th, 20:00.7), Soren Thusholt (37th, 20:19.7), and Trevin Peterson (39th, 20:25.3).\nLittle Falls ran at the Crosby-Ironton Invite at Ruttger’s Bay Lake Lodge on Thursday, Oct. 2, but no results were available at press time.",
